## Tracker state
Table `Applications` = `A1:S2`, headers end with `Folder` (column S). Row 2 is the empty seed row with the Days_Since_Applied formula in P2. Dropdowns cover whole columns E, F, J, M, Q. User keeps it closed while the engine runs.

## Testing conventions
- Never run against the real tracker; copy it to `%TEMP%\htp_ui`, write a config there (incl. `candidate_context_path` to a fictional context) and set `HTP_CONFIG`.
- Start the API without `--reload` from a background shell when testing from the agent; restart it after backend edits. Seed sessions/files via the API since the Cursor browser cannot pick files.
- Keep scratch tests outside the repo; `git status` must stay clean of test artifacts.
